# Package Management with Bun

This workspace uses **bun** as the package manager and runtime for installing dependencies and running commands.

## Installation Commands

Always use `bun` instead of `npm`, `yarn`, or `pnpm`:

```bash
# ✅ CORRECT
bun install
bun add <package>
bun add -d <package>  # for dev dependencies
bun remove <package>

# ❌ INCORRECT
npm install
yarn add <package>
pnpm install
```

## Running Scripts

Use `bun` to run scripts defined in `package.json`:

```bash
# ✅ CORRECT
bun run <script-name>
bun run dev
bun run build
bun run test

# ❌ INCORRECT
npm run <script-name>
yarn <script-name>
pnpm run <script-name>
```

## Direct Execution

Bun can also directly execute TypeScript, JavaScript, and other files:

```bash
# ✅ CORRECT
bun <file.ts>
bun <file.js>

# ❌ INCORRECT
node <file.js>
ts-node <file.ts>
```

## When Suggesting Commands

When suggesting terminal commands to install dependencies or run scripts:
- Always use `bun` instead of other package managers
- Use `bun install` for installing all dependencies
- Use `bun add` for adding new packages
- Use `bun run` for executing scripts from package.json
